HST Office: acceptance tests of HST Sheets dynamic arrays, written by the spec author from the behaviour spec,
independent of the engine's own tests (hst-sheets-dynamic-array-engine.patch).

Test: CppunitTest_sc_hst_dynamic_array_acceptance: any array result spills when typed (one undo step, no
selection left, a single value does not spill), #SPILL! with a blocker and after it is cleared, another array
formula in the way gives #SPILL!, UNIQUE grows and shrinks, A1# / $A$1# (SUM, COUNT, A1#*10, #REF! without an
array, error constants untouched; a one-cell dynamic array is a spill range and grows, a constant or a
single-value formula is not), merged cells and a Sheets table block a spill (a database range without a
table style does not), @ (implicit intersection, @SEQUENCE, #VALUE!), .xlsx export (cm, ref,
_xlfn.ANCHORARRAY, _xlfn.SINGLE, metadata.xml, no cm on a Ctrl+Shift+Enter array) and import of a file written
like the leading spreadsheet application writes it, and Spill.xlsx saved by that application.
